// Transformer.fol — package source file
// Spec: language-ref.md > Type Classes > Transformer
// Grammar: generic-parameter, generic-arity-clause
//
// `F(_)` and `G(_)` declare higher-kinded parameters of arity one: each stands
// for a type constructor that takes one type argument. That is what lets a
// transformer move a value from one structure into a different one.

@co.dap.typeclass(kind=Transformer)
_(F(_), G(_)) co.lang.typeclass = {
    map(value F(A), f (A)->B)->(G(B));
}
